Description: Patrone Sans, Patrone's interface typeface
 Patrone Sans is Noto Sans with a tailed l and a slashed zero, so that I, l,
 1, O and 0 are easy to tell apart in passwords, codes and file names. It
 keeps Noto Sans's look, spacing and line height, and its Latin, Greek and
 Cyrillic. It comes as two variable fonts, upright and italic, with every
 weight from thin to black, medium and semibold among them.
 .
 Pick it in Patrone Settings (Theme, Font) or GNOME Settings' Patrone page.
